% n12: a reference to a LARGER id that is nevertheless already defined --
% node 3 is written before node 2, so the "undefined node" check does not fire
% and only the STRICTLY-SMALLER rule can catch it. Added because mutation
% testing showed n07 was caught by the undefined-node check instead, so it did
% not discriminate the ordering invariant at all.
1 sort 0
3 sort 0
2 pi 3 1
